ace a wooden block on the front end of engine to support the motorcycle and ensure front wheel is oﬀ the ground by minimum 5 cm."}, {"sectionId": "front-wheel-removal-alloy-wheel", "name": "wooden piece", "kind": "size", "value": "4 mm", "unit": "mm", "page": 67, "quote": "Place a 4 mm thick wooden piece or cardboard sheet between the brake pads to avoid pads activation in the event the front brake lever is accidently pressed."}, {"sectionId": "front-wheel-reassembly-alloy-wheel", "name": "axle nut", "kind": "torque", "value": "70 Nm", "unit": "Nm", "page": 68, "quote": "Hold the wheel axle ﬁrmly on right side and tighten axle nut ﬁrmly on right side to a torque of 70 Nm."}, {"sectionId": "front-wheel-reassembly-alloy-wheel", "name": "pinch bolt", "kind": "torque", "value": "25 Nm", "unit": "Nm", "page": 68, "quote": "Tighten pinch bolt completely on fork end to a torque of 25 Nm."}, {"sectionId": "rear-wheel-removal-alloy-wheel", "name": "rear wheel", "kind": "clearance", "value": "6 inches", "unit": "inches", "page": 69, "quote": "Ensure motorcycle is upright on a ﬁrm and ﬂat surface with the rear wheel atleast 6 inches raised above from the surface."}, {"sectionId": "minor-maintenance-tips-71", "name": "Rear wheel spindle hex nut", "kind": "torque", "value": "70 Nm", "unit": "Nm", "page": 71, "quote": "Hold spindle ﬁrmly on left side and tighten hex nut on right side set torque to 70 Nm."}, {"sectionId": "front-wheel-assembly-spokes-wheel", "name": "axle nut torque", "kind": "torque", "value": "70 Nm", "unit": "Nm", "page": 73, "quote": "Hold the wheel axle ﬁrmly on right side and tighten axle nut ﬁrmly on right side to a torque of 70 Nm."}, {"sectionId": "front-wheel-assembly-spokes-wheel", "name": "pinch bolt torque", "kind": "torque", "value": "25 Nm", "unit": "Nm", "page": 73, "quote": "Tighten pinch bolt completely on fork end to a torque of 25 Nm."}, {"sectionId": "clutch-lever-free-play-specification", "name": "Clutch lever free play at LH position", "kind": "clearance", "value": "9-12 mm", "unit": "mm", "page": 77, "quote": "and should be 9-12 mm when handlebars are at LH position"}, {"sectionId": "clutch-lever-free-play-specification", "name": "Clutch lever free play straight", "kind": "clearance", "value": "10-20 mm", "unit": "mm", "page": 77, "quote": "should be checked at 10-20 mm"}, {"sectionId": "drive-chain-tension-free-play-20-30-mm", "name": "Drive chain free play", "kind": "clearance", "value": "20 to 30 mm", "unit": "mm", "page": 78, "quote": "The drive chain free play is 20 to 30 mm."}, {"sectionId": "battery-maintenance", "name": "battery", "kind": "capacity", "value": "12 V - 12 Ah V - Ah", "unit": "V - Ah", "page": 79, "quote": "The Motorcycle is provided with 12 V - 12 Ah battery."}, {"sectionId": "headlamp-dismantling", "name": "headlamp rim screws", "kind": "other", "value": "2 Nos", "page": 84, "quote": "Gently loosen and remove the headlamp rim screws 2 Nos from headlamp cowl by using screwdriver available in the tool kit"}, {"sectionId": "headlamp-dismantling", "name": "head lamp holding clips", "kind": "other", "value": "4 nos", "page": 84, "quote": "Gently release the headlamp holding clips 4 nos from head lamp rim."}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Alternator fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "30 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "1 GN 30 A Alternator"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Main Fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "30 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "2 GN 30 A Main Fuse"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Ignition Fuse-EFI", "kind": "electrical", "value": "15 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "3 BU 15 A Ignition Fuse-EFI"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Signalling Fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "10 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "4 RD 10 A Signalling Fuse"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Horn Fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "10 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "5 RD 10 A Horn Fuse"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Lighting Fuse (Head Lamp)", "kind": "electrical", "value": "15 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "6 BU 15 A Lighting Fuse (Head Lamp)"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "Accessory Fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "10 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "7 RD 10 A Accessory Fuse"}, {"sectionId": "mini-blade-fuse-usage-list", "name": "ABS Fuse", "kind": "electrical", "value": "10 A", "unit": "A", "page": 89, "quote": "8 RD 10 A ABS Fuse"}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Adjuster steps", "kind": "other", "value": "5 step", "unit": "step", "page": 92, "quote": "The adjuster is a 5 step adjuster and it is kept at first notch position."}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Rider payload", "kind": "capacity", "value": "90 kg", "unit": "kg", "page": 93, "quote": "Rider upto 90 kg"}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Maximum payload", "kind": "capacity", "value": "180 kg", "unit": "kg", "page": 93, "quote": "Upto a maximum of 180 kg payload (Inc of rider weight, pillion weight and accessories)"}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Front tyre pressure, unladen / one up", "kind": "pressure", "value": "32 psi", "unit": "psi", "page": 93, "quote": "Unladen / One up Loading / Rider only. Rider upto 90 kg 1st 32 36"}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Rear tyre pressure, unladen / one up", "kind": "pressure", "value": "36 psi", "unit": "psi", "page": 93, "quote": "Unladen / One up Loading / Rider only. Rider upto 90 kg 1st 32 36"}, {"sectionId": "rear-suspension-setting", "name": "Front tyre pressure, laden / two up", "kind": "pressure", "value": "32 psi", "unit": "psi", "page": 93, "quote": "Laden / Two up / Rider + Pillions / Rider + Pillion + Accessories Upto a maximum of 180 kg payload (Inc of rider weight, pillion weight and accessories) 5th 32 39"}, {"sectio